# N6 (b): L->R chains: sum_k I_k, I_k = I(A_1..A_{k-1} : A_{k+1} | A_k) (lattice vacuum), the
# continuum (1/3) log 1/(1-eta_k), and Phi_tot/(sum_k I_k / 2).
# N6 (c): equal-block chains l = (1,...,1) m, n_blocks = 2..6 (n_blocks = 2: no step, Phi_tot = 0 exactly);
# zeta_k^(I) = (k-1)(n-k+1)/n; SA = 2 sum_k Phi_A(zeta_k) (no cross terms).

eq2 (n_blocks = 2): the L->R chain has no step (the starting block A_1A_2 is the whole chain), so
  the recovered state is the vacuum and Phi_tot = D_tot = 0 exactly at every size.

